@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #9ca3af

title One FindCare search end to end: the router carries the words, the page mines them, writes them, reads back what is in force, and either searches or asks

participant "Router\nuniversal_navigation_tool" as UR
participant "Search route\n/facility/find" as Route
participant "Miner\nmine_facility_parameters" as Miner
participant "SpecialtyFilter\nNon-Individual partition" as Cat
database "Session\nuserParameters.pages.facility" as Session
participant "Declaration\nToolConfiguration" as Decl
database "Provider\ncollection" as Providers

note over UR, Route
  Reference implementation: /facility/find in
  Code/ConversationalUX/FindCareChat/backend/app.py.
  The individual-provider and NUCC pages are the same
  six steps against their own page and their own tool.
end note

UR -> UR : latest_utterance_and_prior_dialogue()\nthe last thing said, and the talk before it
note left of UR
  The router reads no parameter and forms no opinion
  about what the words mean. Its whole part in a mining
  turn is producing those two things.
end note

UR -> Route : POST { session_token, utterance, history }
activate Route
Route -> Route : require_gateway_signature()

Route -> Miner : mine(utterance, history)
activate Miner
Miner --> Route : geography, facilityType,\nfacilityName
deactivate Miner

alt a kind of place was named
  Route -> Cat : find_specialties(facilityType,\nSection = Non-Individual)
  activate Cat
  Cat --> Route : offered kinds + codes
  deactivate Cat
end

Route -> Session : $set pages.facility.<attribute>\nroute = tool, determination = model
note right of Session
  Written before the search runs, so what the answer
  was produced under is on the session whatever the
  search then does.
end note

Route -> Session : read every parameter this page holds
Session --> Route : in_force
note right of Route
  What the search runs on is what is in force, not what
  this turn happened to say. A person who named a city
  one turn and a state the next has given both.
end note

Route -> Providers : state of the ZIP, when no state was said
Providers --> Route : derived state
note right of Route
  Derived for the requirement check only. The query is
  still built from what was asked for: the ZIP is
  narrower than the state it implies.
end note

Route -> Decl : required_parameters("FacilitySearch")
Decl --> Route : state, selectedTaxonomyCodes
Route -> Route : unmet = those not in force

alt nothing unmet
  Route -> Providers : search_providers(entity_type = "2", codes, place)
  Providers --> Route : rows + total
else something unmet
  Route -> Route : ask_for_missing(tool, unmet,\noptional, in_force, utterance)
  note right of Route
    The tool authors the question because the tool holds
    the requirement. Making a parameter Required is an
    edit to the record and a deploy, not a line of code.
  end note
end

Route --> UR : rows, mined, unmet_requirements,\nrefinement_question
deactivate Route

@enduml
